1797:### String and float conversion
1798-
1799:You can convert between a `String` and a `Float`. The String will be
1800-represented in the syntax of the `Float` sort (see the section on the `FLOAT`
1801-module above for details of that syntax). Which particular string is returned
1802:by `Float2String` is determined by the backend, but the same `Float` is
1803:guaranteed to return the same `String`, and converting that `String` back to a
1804-`Float` is guaranteed to return the original `Float`.
1805-
1806-You can also convert a `Float` to a string in a particular syntax using the
1807:variant of `Float2String` with a `format`. In this case, the resulting string
1808-is one which results directly from passing that `format` to `mpfr_printf`. This
1809-functionality may not be supported on backends that do not use Gnu MPFR to
1810-implement floating-point numbers.
