1819-
1820:You can convert between a `String` and an `Int`. The String will be represented
1821-in the syntax of the `INT` module (i.e., a nonempty sequence of digits
1822:optionally prefixed by a sign). When converting from an `Int` to a `String`,
1823-the sign will not be present unless the integer is negative.
1824-
1825:You can also convert between a `String` and an `Int` in a particular radix.
1826-This radix can be anywhere between 2 and 36. For a radix 2 <= N <= 10, the
1827-digits 0 to N-1 will be used. For a radix 11 <= N <= 36, the digits 0 to 9
1828-and the first N-10 letters of the Latin alphabet will be used. Both uppercase
1829:and lowercase letters are supported by `String2Base`. Whether the letters
1830:returned by `Base2String` are upper or lowercase is determined by the backend,
1831-but the backend will consistently choose one or the other.
